---
import Card from '../Card.astro';
import LiveDemo from './LiveDemo.astro';
import { docsUrl, repositorySource } from '../../../docs.mjs';
---

<section id="apps">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Apps</span>
      <h2>Cross-platform UI</h2>
      <p class="kicker">Change the code. The app keeps going.</p>
      <p class="lede">
        Run your app with <code>haxeon run --watch</code> and save a change: the running app takes
        the new code and keeps what it was doing. Try it here: click a few times, then apply the
        edit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <LiveDemo />
    <div class="steps">
      <span><b>Patched in place:</b> logic, data, native calls and UI.</span><span>
        <b>Kept:</b> every object the app made.
      </span><span><b>A broken edit:</b> the app keeps running the last good code.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="grid three capabilities">
      <Card>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"></rect><path d="M3 9h18M9 9v10"></path>
          </svg><h3>UI that looks the same everywhere</h3>
        </div><p class="detail">
          The <a href="/ui/"><code>ui</code> package</a> draws on the GPU,
          with real text handling built in. Draw your own scenes beside it with
          the <a href="/gpu/">GPU layer</a>.
        </p><div class="chips">
          <span>Layout</span><span>Text shaping</span><span>Right-to-left text</span><span>
            CJK line breaking
          </span><span>Vector drawing</span><span>Themes</span>
        </div>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 16v-5a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v5l1.5 2h-15z"></path><path d="M10 20.5a2 2 0 0 0 4 0"
            ></path>
          </svg><h3>Native services from the OS</h3>
        </div><p class="detail">
          Each platform's own services, through one <a
            href={repositorySource('packages/platform')}
          >
            NativeKit API
          </a>.
        </p><div class="chips">
          <span>Windows</span><span>Menus</span><span>Tray</span><span>Dialogs</span><span>
            Notifications
          </span><span>Clipboard</span><span>WebView</span><span>Accessibility</span><span>
            Gamepad
          </span><span>Sensors</span><span>File watching</span><span>Networking</span>
        </div>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 3l8 4.5v9L12 21l-8-4.5v-9z"></path><path d="M4 7.5l8 4.5 8-4.5M12 12v9"
            ></path>
          </svg><h3>Packages</h3>
        </div><p class="detail">
          From the <a href={docsUrl('reference/MANIFEST.md') + '#the-haxeon-registry'}
            >haxeon registry</a
          >, versioned with the toolchain.
        </p><div class="chips">
          {
            [
              'gpu',
              'audio',
              'animation',
              'editor',
              'filesystem',
              'credentials',
              'platform',
              'agentkit',
            ].map((name) => <a href={name === 'gpu' ? '/gpu/' : repositorySource('packages/' + name)}>{name}</a>)
          }
        </div>
      </Card>
    </div>
    <p class="note">NativeKit is experimental and pre-1.0. Its ABI is still evolving.</p>

    <div class="ctas">
      <a class="btn primary" href={docsUrl('guides/01-first-app.md')}>Build your first app</a><a
        class="btn ghost"
        href={repositorySource('docs/guides/examples/03-ui-basics/tasks/')}
      >
        Get the demo source
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--hx-space-5);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    margin-top: var(--hx-space-5);
  }
  .steps b {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .capabilities {
    margin-top: var(--hx-space-7);
  }
  .chips span,
  .chips a {
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: var(--hx-radius-pill);
    background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
</style>
